  "grammarNotes": [
    {
      "id": "familie-articles",
      "title": "der, die, das",
      "body": "Every German noun has a gender, shown by its article:\n\n- **der**: masculine (the app shows these in blue)\n- **die**: feminine (red)\n- **das**: neuter (green)\n\nAlways learn a noun **with** its article: not *Kind*, but *das Kind*.\n\nSome patterns help:\n\n- Male people are usually *der*: der Vater, der Sohn\n- Female people are usually *die*: die Mutter, die Tochter\n- Words ending in **-chen** are always *das*: **das Mädchen** (the girl)\n\nIn the plural, the article is always **die**."
    },
    {
      "id": "familie-possessives",
      "title": "my, your, his, her",
      "body": "Possessives add **-e** before a *die* word and before plurals. Before *der* and *das* words they have no ending.\n\nThe ending depends on the noun that **follows**, not on the owner: *Tom und seine Schwester*, *Lena und ihr Bruder*.",
      "table": [
        ["", "der / das word", "die word / plural"],
        ["my", "mein Vater", "meine Mutter"],
        ["your (informal)", "dein Bruder", "deine Schwester"],
        ["your (formal)", "Ihr Sohn", "Ihre Tochter"],
        ["his", "sein Kind", "seine Kinder"],
        ["her", "ihr Mann", "ihre Eltern"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "familie-plurals",
      "title": "Plurals",
      "body": "German has several plural patterns, so learn each noun's plural along with it. Many plurals also add an umlaut.",
      "table": [
        ["Pattern", "Singular", "Plural"],
        ["-e / ¨e", "der Sohn", "die Söhne"],
        ["-er / ¨er", "das Kind", "die Kinder"],
        ["-n / -en", "die Schwester", "die Schwestern"],
        ["-s", "die Oma", "die Omas"],
        ["no ending", "der Onkel", "die Onkel"],
        ["umlaut only", "der Vater", "die Väter"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "familie-das-ist",
      "title": "Das ist … / Das sind …",
      "body": "Use **Das ist** for one person or thing and **Das sind** for more than one:\n\n- *Das ist mein Bruder.* This is my brother.\n- *Das sind meine Eltern.* These are my parents.\n\n**die Eltern** (parents) only exists in the plural."
    }
  ],
