          "id": "f4-e1",
          "type": "TEACH",
          "title": "One, two, many",
          "body": "In the plural, the article is always **die**, whatever the gender: *der Bruder → die Brüder*.\n\nGerman has several plural patterns, so learn each noun's plural with it:\n\n- add **-e**, often with an umlaut: der Sohn → die S**ö**hn**e**\n- add **-er**: das Kind → die Kind**er**\n- add **-n** or **-en**: die Tante → die Tante**n**\n- add **-s**: die Oma → die Oma**s**\n- no ending, sometimes an umlaut: der Onkel → die Onkel, der Vater → die V**ä**ter",
          "examples": [
            { "text": "die Söhne", "translation": "the sons" },
            { "text": "die Kinder", "translation": "the children" },
            { "text": "die Tanten", "translation": "the aunts" },
            { "text": "die Omas", "translation": "the grandmas" },
            { "text": "die Väter", "translation": "the fathers" }
